The audit shows the listed method names are mostly aliases or inlined logic, but I found one real vanilla behavior gap on the live `tryPlaceLeaf` path: Pumpkin only sets `waterlogged=true` when water is present, while vanilla explicitly writes the waterlogged property to the fluid-source boolean (including forcing `false`). I’ll fix that existing caller path and add a focused test if the local cache test harness supports it; the remaining leads will be recorded with exact classifications and grep evidence.
