The packet class has no genuine gap: every absent Java name is already represented by the Rust packet/codec or generated packet metadata, and live waypoint command code calls the Rust constructors. Cartography is the real behavioral gap: the existing handler routes clicks but never refreshes the result or consumes inputs on result-take. I’m wiring the vanilla map-copy path into the existing `on_slot_click`/`quick_move` call chain and adding a result-slot callback plus a focused test. Scale/lock post-processing remains a separate limitation because this workspace’s marker component has no operation payload or crafted-map consumer; I’ll document the exact grep evidence.
